the Game of Thrones guys are getting out  of the galaxy far far away David Benioff  and DB Weiss best known for creating and  showrunning game of Thrones have exited  Lucasfilm and their planned Star Wars  trilogy the pair were slated to write  and direct three films that would have  served as the next chapter in the Star  Wars franchise following the launch of  the rise of Skywalker the final  installment in the nine film Skywalker  saga Benioff and Weiss revealed in a  statement why they are no longer making  their Star Wars trilogy they are simply  too busy working on projects for Netflix  in August 2019 it was reported that the  duo had inked a massive five-year deal  believed to be worth as much as 300  million dollars with the streaming giant  to create new television series and  original movies no details on Benioff  and Weiss as Netflix shows and films  have been revealed as of the making of  this video but it seems clear that they  may be more invested in those projects  than in their three Star Wars films  still the joint statement that Benioff  and Weiss provided to Deadline alongside  the announcement indicates that their  decision to depart from the Star Wars  universe had no ill intent and that the  move wasn't motivated by any bad blood  or behind-the-scenes troubles it read in  part we love Star Wars when George Lucas  built it he built us - getting to talk  about Star Wars with him and the current  Star Wars team was the thrill of a  lifetime and we will always be indebted  to the saga that changed everything  there are only so many hours in the day  and we felt we could not do justice to  both Star Wars and our Netflix projects  so we are regretfully stepping away  Lucasfilm president Kathleen Kennedy  echoed Benioff and Weiss his sentiments  in a statement of her own writing David  Benioff and Dan Weiss are incredible  storytellers we hope to include them in  the journey forward when they are able  to step away from their busy schedule to  focus on Star Wars judging by the  remarks Veni off Weiss and Kennedy made  it appears that everything is pretty  peachy keen between the creatives and  the studio  however some Thrones fans have begun  theorizing that perhaps this isn't the  entire truth and that lucasville may  have actually fired Benioff and Weiss  over their polarizing handling of the  final season of Game of Thrones  my heart is broken don't touch me  this of course is all just speculation  the upside of all of this is that the  Star Wars franchise will be just fine  without Benioff and Weiss on board  Lucasfilm is far smarter than to have  the future success of the entire film  series hinge on the enduring commitment  of two people plus the studio has plenty  of time to get its proverbial Tie  Fighters in a row and decide who should  take the reins on the franchise moving  forward as the Star Wars films we'll be  taking a brief hiatus following the  December 20th premiere of the rise of  Skywalker it's believed that the break  will last three years given that the  first of Benioff and Weiss as three Star  Wars installments was expected to hit  cinemas sometime in 2022 one might  assume that Lucasfilm would have to  delay the franchise return by a year or  two to make up for the loss of Benioff  and Weiss and creative shakeups that  will ensue but don't forget that the  studio has two big-name movie makers  already working on projects of their own  creatives who are more than capable of  taking the place of Benioff and Weiss  both the last Jedi writer director Rian  Johnson and Marvel Studios chief  creative officer Kevin Feige are set to  create their own additions to the Star  Wars universe with Johnson making his  own trilogy and Feige onboard to produce  one movie it seems most plausible that  Lucasfilm will effectively replace  Benioff and Weiss as trilogy with  Johnston's though there's no way to know  what the studio will do at this point in  time either way the future of Star Wars  still looks bright check out one of our  newest videos right here plus even more  looper videos about Star Wars are coming  soon subscribe to our YouTube channel  and hit the belts so you don't miss a  single one  [Music]
 

